 placeholder value; instrument is missing or a placeholder value; justification is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the Disposition claim that 'the drift report and admitted specs are the only files written' with the ledger `finalize()` writes — e.g. scope it to 'the only NEW result artifacts; the epic ledger.jsonl is appended by finalize()'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["COH"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4937,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the drift report and admitted specs are the only files written'","'then `finalize()`s priced ACTUAL usage' / 'a criterion is done iff its stable `run_id` is in the ledger'"],"finding":"The Disposition section states 'the drift report and admitted specs are the only files written', but the Budget-enforcement and Failure-disposition sections describe `finalize()` writing priced actual-usage rows to the epic's `ledger.jsonl` and the ledger being 'the sole resume oracle'. These two statements contradict each other about what files the run writes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f05ee6c8f87adcff3","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Disposition vs Budget enforcement / Failure disposition","norm_id":"nca438cb7107a2e10","priority":0.3063,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads 'only files written' and omits ledger persistence, breaking resume; or notices the contradiction and stops to ask which is authoritative."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword Disposition to: 'the drift report, admitted specs, and appended ledger rows are the only writes; no other files are produced.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Surface retry-exhausted/incomplete criteria in the run summary (e.g. an `incomplete`/`errored` id list) or as a drift-report entry, so an attempted-but-abandoned criterion is observably distinct from a clean skip.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A transient model/transport error is RETRYABLE (3×, exp backoff 1s/2s/4s); on exhaustion the criterion is left incomplete (no ledger row; run continues).'","'The runner returns an in-memory summary (admitted/withheld ids, drift entries, spend); the drift report and admitted specs are the only files written.'","ABSENCE: no summary field, log, or drift-report classification is specified for criteria that were attempted but abandoned after retry exhaustion — the error state is surfaced only as an absence of any record."],"finding":"On transient-error retry exhaustion the criterion is 'left incomplete (no ledger row; run continues)', but the plan's in-memory summary only enumerates admitted ids, withheld ids, drift entries, and spend — a retry-exhausted criterion falls into none of these buckets and is not written to the drift report, so an operator has no signal that a criterion silently failed to be processed at all (distinct from a legitimate skip or a non-reproduction).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb502e9d5ee832816","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Failure disposition — 'on exhaustion the criterion is left incomplete (no ledger row; run continues)'; and Approach — 'returns an in-memory summary (admitted/withheld ids, drift entries, spend)'","norm_id":"ne2ae5def0919dd24","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A live admission run where two criteria hit persistent throttling: they retry-exhaust, produce no ledger row, no spec, and no drift entry — the operator sees a green run and assumes those criteria had no candidates, never learning coverage was silently lost."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an `incomplete` bucket to the in-memory summary listing criteria abandoned after retry exhaustion (with the terminal error), so operators can distinguish transport failure from no-candidate/skip.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the runner disposes of a criterion whose finder is not runnable over inline sidecar-replay material (e.g. ISF/session-log finders, or a container criterion with no children): skip like a shadowed built-in AND emit a drift entry, rather than letting eval_solver.run_case's ValueError crash the run.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: runner 'runs the criterion's current Pass-1 finder via eval_solver.run_case(...)'; the only enumerated skip is the no-shadowing packaged built-in guard.","eval_solver.py:141-145: `if cid in INLINE_UNADMISSIBLE_CRITERIA: raise ValueError(... 'not runnable over an inline eval fixture')`; also container criteria with no children raise ValueError (eval_solver.py:122-126).","Plan failure disposition only categorizes transient (RETRYABLE 3x) and budget (FATAL) errors — a ValueError from run_case matches neither, so it propagates uncaught.","ABSENCE: the plan names no disposition for a criterion whose finder cannot run over the rehydrated inline material, though such criteria can appear in the selector manifest."],"finding":"The plan runs eval_solver.run_case over every non-shadowed criterion but does not handle criteria whose Pass-1 finder is not runnable over inline sidecar-replay material (e.g. ISF finders needing a real session log). run_case raises a plain ValueError for these, which is neither the plan's RETRYABLE transient class nor its FATAL budget class, so an unclassified exception would crash the whole admission run mid-way, abandoning already-finalized criteria.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f07ddacb9005fd7b2","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach § 'Rehydrate, then run.' / 'No-shadowing guard.' / 'Failure disposition.'","norm_id":"n48f525101d423527","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The selector manifest lists an ISF (session-log) criterion among candidates.","A container criterion resolves to a row with no children, so run_case raises before any verdict."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a pre-dispatch skip: before running a criterion, exclude any id in eval_solver.INLINE_UNADMISSIBLE_CRITERIA (and treat a missing/empty container `children` payload as a withheld/drift case), recording each as a drift entry with an explanatory reason so the run stays auditable and non-fatal.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_imp